30,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"It seems we are spending quite a bit on supplies, and the billing for professional services is centralized to one person. This creates an imbalance in who is out of pocket.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The time required for a full pass is significant, and professional firms have rigid terms. We need to consider if the time saved is worth the cost.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"My research shows a disparity between who uses the space and who is actually present. Some of us are barely here, yet the workload remains shared.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,1,talk,May,,"The standard of ""clean"" varies wildly between us, and the bathroom has a ventilation issue that makes it get dirty again almost immediately.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,1,talk,Midori,,"It's sad to see that our arguments usually stem from reminders about chores. Even the previous tenants struggled with permanent divisions, eventually stopping speaking to each other.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Benjamin, if usage is uneven, a flat split of labor might be perceived as unfair. However, we must ensure the financial side is settled clearly.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@May, if the bathroom degrades in less than two weeks regardless of effort, a strict rota might just lead to frustration without improving the state of the room.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Toshio, exactly. A system that ignores the actual presence of housemates is logically flawed. We need a solution that accounts for the actual burden.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,May,,"@Ryuji, that's my fear. If we don't agree on what ""done"" means, we'll just keep arguing regardless of who is assigned to the room.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@May, that's why harmony is so important. If we focus too much on the rules and not the relationship, we'll end up like the previous tenants.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Midori, while harmony is a goal, it cannot be achieved without a fair distribution of costs. We cannot have one person funding the supplies for everyone.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"I am concerned about the total hours. If we don't outsource, the time commitment is substantial. We need to know if we can actually handle the workload.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Ryuji, the workload is only a burden if it's distributed poorly. If we align the work with the usage, the ""hours"" become less of an issue.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,3,talk,May,,I just want to stop guessing if the kitchen is grim. A system that guarantees a certain standard is more important to me than who does it.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Midori,,I agree with May. A predictable environment reduces the need for those stressful reminders that lead to rows in the chat.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
