55,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"We have three options: Standing Assignments, a Paid Cleaning Service, or a Fixed Weekly Rota. Given the financial mess, a professional service with a clear invoice is appealing.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"Option B removes the labor burden entirely, which is the most rational way to avoid the time-sink I'm worried about. I prefer the professional route.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Option C is the most traditionally fair, but Option B removes the conflict over usage and presence entirely. It's the most logical way to maintain peace.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,1,talk,May,,"Option B is the only one that guarantees a professional standard. I won't have to worry about different definitions of ""clean"" or the bathroom grout.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,1,talk,Midori,,I worry that Option A might lead to the same silence the previous tenants experienced. Option B takes the pressure off us and keeps us as friends.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Midori, I agree. If we pay a service, the financial transaction is clear and the labor is gone. It solves both the money and the mood issues.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Benjamin, do you agree that removing the labor is better than trying to calculate usage-based rotas, which would be a logistical nightmare?","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Ryuji, yes. The administrative effort to balance usage against labor is higher than the cost of a service. Option B is the most efficient.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,2,talk,May,,I'm fully on board with Option B. It's the only way to ensure the bathroom doesn't become a place I have to brace myself for.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,2,talk,Midori,,"It seems we are all leaning toward the same thing. As long as we split the cost fairly, I think this is the kindest choice for our home.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,3,talk,Toshio,,I will vote for Option B. It provides a clear billing structure and eliminates the dispute over who bought the last bottle of spray.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,I vote for Option B. It is the only option that realistically addresses the time commitment required for a proper clean.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,I vote for Option B. It is the most rational solution to the disparity in housemate presence and usage.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,3,talk,May,,"I vote for Option B! No more guessing, no more grim kitchens, just a professional clean.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,3,talk,Midori,,I vote for Option B as well. Let's prioritize our friendship over the chores.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
